<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH 1996 C/A DEFICIT GROWS TO $4.48 BLN.</title>
<headline>CZECH 1996 C/A DEFICIT GROWS TO $4.48 BLN.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Republic's current account balance ended 1996 with a deficit of $4.476 billion, compared to a $1.362 billion shortfall in 1995, the central bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It added in a statement that according to preliminary results, the 1996 capital account ended with a $4.072 billion surplus, after an $8.226 billion surplus for the previous year.</p>
</text>
